  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Direct Variation 4 - Graph (interactive)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The cost, \(C\), of maize (in hundreds of Ksh) varies directly as its mass, \(m\), in kg: \(C = km\). The graph shows this relationship, and \(P\) is a point on the line.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans2="ans2Ref" width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
board.create('text', [8.3, 1.5, 'm (kg)'], {fixed:true});
board.create('text', [0.2, 36.5, 'C (Ksh 100s)'], {fixed:true});
var line = board.create('line', [[0,0],[1,{#pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
var P = board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pk*pr#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4});
var A = board.create('point', [1,1], {name:'A', snapToGrid:true, snapSizeX:1, snapSizeY:1, size:5});
stack_jxg.bind_point(ans2Ref, A);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>(a) Use the point \(P\) to find the constant \(k\), in hundreds of Ksh per kg.</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Drag the point \(A\) to the point on the line where \(m = {@px2@}\) kg. The coordinates of \(A\) appear in the box below.</p>
<p>\(A = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<h4>(a) Find the constant \(k\)</h4>
<p><strong>Step 1: read the coordinates of \(P\) from the graph.</strong> \(P\) is at \(m = {@pr@}\) on the horizontal axis and \(C = {@pk*pr@}\) on the vertical axis, so \(P = ({@pr@}, {@pk*pr@})\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: substitute these values into \(C = km\).</strong></p>
\[ {@pk*pr@} = k \times {@pr@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 3: divide both sides by \({@pr@}\).</strong> \(k\) is multiplied by \({@pr@}\), so dividing by \({@pr@}\) leaves \(k\) on its own:</p>
\[ k = \frac{ {@pk*pr@} }{ {@pr@} } = {@pk@}. \]
<p>Because \(C\) is measured in hundreds of Ksh, maize costs \({@pk@}\) hundred Ksh, that is Ksh \({@100*pk@}\), per kilogram.</p>

<h4>(b) Find the point \(A\) on the line where \(m = {@px2@}\)</h4>
<p><strong>Step 1: write the equation of the line using \(k\) from part (a).</strong></p>
\[ C = {@pk@}m. \]
<p><strong>Step 2: substitute \(m = {@px2@}\).</strong></p>
\[ C = {@pk@} \times {@px2@} = {@pk*px2@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 3: write down the coordinates of \(A\).</strong> On the graph, go along the horizontal axis to \(m = {@px2@}\), then straight up to the line. The line is at \(C = {@pk*px2@}\), so</p>
\[ A = ({@px2@}, {@pk*px2@}). \]

[[jsxgraph width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
board.create('line', [[0,0],[1,{#pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pk*pr#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4, label:{offset:[-10,10], anchorX:'right'}});
board.create('point', [{#px2#},{#pk*px2#}], {name:'A', fixed:true, color:'green', size:4, label:{offset:[10,-10], anchorX:'left'}});
board.create('segment', [[{#px2#},0],[{#px2#},{#pk*px2#}]], {dash:2, strokeColor:'#888', fixed:true});
board.create('segment', [[0,{#pk*px2#}],[{#px2#},{#pk*px2#}]], {dash:2, strokeColor:'#888', fixed:true});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
